        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(7) After an applicant has drawn and used thirty (30) consecutive sick leave days (determined by his/her duty days) from the bank, he/she shall be given a medical review by a physician of the administering committee's choice, at the contributor's expense. The physician's report is to be sent directly to the committee before the committee may act upon his/her application for an extension of use of the sick leave bank. Such medical review may be eliminated by the committee if the applicant has been confined to a hospital or other medical facility through the prior thirty (30) days he/she has used the sick leave bank.",
            "block_bbox": [
                156,
                175,
                711,
                421
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
